From: Trent Brown <trent.brown@adtran.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 15:00:26 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] iw: util: read the EHT PHY capabilities from a buffer of full size

The EHT PHY Capabilities field has 9 bytes. __print_eht_capa() prints
all 9 and reads the field as three 32-bit words, so the third word
covers bytes 8 to 11. For a scan element of minimum length, the last
of these bytes lies after the element. For "iw phy", print_eht_info()
copies the field into a buffer of 8 bytes, so the ninth byte and the
two "QAM In Wider Bandwidth" flags come from the stack.

In both callers, copy the field into a zeroed buffer of three words.

Fixes: 4c859917316b ("iw: util: update and clean up eht capa printing")
Signed-off-by: Trent Brown <trent.brown@adtran.com>
---
 util.c |    8 +++++---
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/util.c
+++ b/util.c
@@ -1723,7 +1723,7 @@ void print_eht_info(struct nlattr *nl_if
 {
 	struct nlattr *tb[NL80211_BAND_IFTYPE_ATTR_MAX + 1];
 	__u8 mac_cap[2] = { 0 };
-	__u32 phy_cap[2] = { 0 };
+	__u32 phy_cap[3] = { 0 };
 	__u8 mcs_set[13] = { 0 };
 	__u8 ppet[31] = { 0 };
 	__u16 he_phy_cap[6] = { 0 };
@@ -1799,14 +1799,16 @@ void print_eht_info(struct nlattr *nl_if
 void print_eht_capability(const uint8_t *ie, int len, const uint8_t *he_cap,
 			  bool from_ap)
 {
-	const void *mac_cap, *phy_cap, *mcs_set, *he_phy_cap;
+	const void *mac_cap, *mcs_set, *he_phy_cap;
+	__u32 phy_cap[3] = { 0 };
 	int mcs_len;
 	int i = 0;
 
 	mac_cap = &ie[i];
 	i += 2;
 
-	phy_cap = &ie[i];
+	/* the 9 bytes are read as three words */
+	memcpy(phy_cap, &ie[i], 9);
 	i += 9;
 
 	mcs_set = &ie[i];
